It was not intended by me to be a "strawman argument".

This is how the statement "every death in nethack is avoidable" in its
most extreme interpretation ("if you die, you have done something
wrong") looks to me.


In principle, the statement ist correct.

For every possible cause of death there is a countermeasure to prevent
it. E.g. being engulfed by a purple worm a =oSD or several different
wands can help you.

But in practice this doesn't always works. Be it that you haven't had
enough time to properly prepare or that the RNG wants to screw you,
there are situations that couldn't be avoided.

With the benefit of hindsight one might say that the death maybe could
have been avoided (as all deaths are in principle avoidable) but
NetHack is - as life - sometimes not fair.

